<ttl id="10006_S000J_744E7_T004T" variety="T004T">
<name>EFI System (2AZ-FE)</name>
<para id="RM0000008Y100OX" category="C" type-id="3007P" name-id="065A4-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>P0500/42</dtccode>
<dtcname>Vehicle Speed Sensor System</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000008Y100OX_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00002P000000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The vehicle speed pulse signal output from the ABS speed sensor installed on each wheel is converted by the skid control computer into a vehicle speed pulse signal (equivalent to 4 pulses per 1 revolution of the transaxle rotating shaft), output to the combination meter assembly as the vehicle speed signal, and input to the engine control computer.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A065387J04" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.06in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.83in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.19in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
<ptxt>SAE/TCCS</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
<ptxt>1. Detection condition 2. Malfunction status 3. Malfunction duration 4. Other</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>P0500/42</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>While driving</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>SPD signal is not input</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>2 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>1 trip</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Wire harness or connector (including instrument panel J/B)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Combination Meter Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Engine Control Computer</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Skid Control Computer Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000008Y100OX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00002P100000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="G100110J12" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000008Y100OX_04" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___00002P700000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If the SPD line branches to other ECUs from an option connector, etc., first disconnect those circuits and inspect.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), read the Freeze Frame Data. Freeze Frame Data records part of the engine operating conditions when a malfunction occurs, and this information is useful for troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000008Y100OX_03" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM0000008Y100OX_03_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___00002P200000">
<scantool type="4"/>
<testtitle>Read TaSCAN Data (Vehicle Speed)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check that the speedometer operates normally.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform a road test of the vehicle.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display, read the Data List item [Vehicle Speed] from [Diagnosis Function Menu] → [ECU Data Monitor].</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>SST (TaSCAN) data monitor display and speedometer display are the same</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000008Y100OX_03_0004" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000008Y100OX_03_0002" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000008Y100OX_03_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___00002P300000">
<testtitle>Inspect Combination Meter System</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Inspect the vehicle speed signal circuit of the meter &amp; gauge system.</ptxt>
</test1>
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the procedure, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002YMX000X"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000008Y100OX_03_0003" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000008Y100OX_03_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___00002P400000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Engine Control Computer - Combination Meter Assembly)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the wire harness and connector inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect connector B of the engine control computer and the combination meter assembly connector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A127855J04" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the engine control computer and combination meter assembly vehicle side connector terminals. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="X39400000QV016D"/> for Terminals of ECU)</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC0" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Name)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B8(SPD) - 36(+S)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B8 (SPD) and 36 (+S) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10k Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000008Y100OX_03_0012" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000008Y100OX_03_0006" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
